<div class="re-ai-editorial">
<section><h2>Use AI to qualify seller inquiries thoughtfully</h2><p>A seller-focused chatbot or AI receptionist can ask about the general property location, the homeowner&#x27;s expected selling timeframe and whether they would like a listing consultation. Those answers can help route the inquiry to an agent familiar with the area.</p><p>An automated assistant should not promise a selling price or present an unsupported valuation as a professional appraisal. Its role is to establish context, explain available next steps and make it easier to begin a genuine conversation.</p></section>
<section><h2>Build follow-up around the homeowner&#x27;s timeline</h2><p>A homeowner considering a sale next month should not receive the same sequence as someone researching a possible move next year. CRM automation can distinguish near-term consultations from longer-term follow-up and create tasks for agents when the prospect expresses stronger interest.</p><p>AI-assisted SMS, email and call workflows can use the person&#x27;s stated interests while respecting permissions and opt-outs. Track confirmed listing consultations and verified signed listings only when the brokerage has reliable records.</p></section>
